1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 e5 5. Nb5 d6 6. c4 Be7 7. N1c3 a6 8. Na3
Be6 9. Be3 Nf6 10. Be2 O-O 11. O-O Rc8 12. Rc1 Na5 13. Qa4 Nxc4 14. Nxc4 b5 15.
Qxa6 bxc4 16. Bb6 Qe8 17. f3 Ra8 18. Qb5 $2 ({White's 18th lost a piece but if
instead} 18. Qb7 Qb8 $1 19. Qxb8 (19. Qxe7 Qxb6+ {and Ra7 traps the queen})
19... Rfxb8 20. Be3 Rxb2 {when Black has an extra pawn with good winning
chances (Barden)}) 18... Qxb5 19. Nxb5 Rab8 {Source: The Guardian, 25 August
1990. N.b.Big/Mega Database 2020 cites this as played by Demis Hassabis in the
Lloyds Bank Masters but it was actually played by his younger brother,
six-year-old George Hassabis as part of the launch of the tournament.} 0-1

